## Architecture Overview

```text
allocation-study-07/
├── pyproject.toml
├── README.md
├── blotto/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── core/
│   │   ├── rules.py         # Validation (sum == 100, 5 castles, non-negative integers) and castle weights [1..5]
│   │   └── scoring.py       # Vectorized NumPy evaluation for 1v1 head-to-head, exact DP, and 4-way pods
│   ├── strategies/
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   ├── base.py          # Abstract Base Class for fixed and stochastic strategies
│   │   ├── archetypes.py    # Hardcoded vectors: final submissions, LLM baselines, Shark vectors, probes
│   │   └── generative.py    # Dirichlet, uniform simplex, and random integer-transfer noise generators
│   ├── sim/
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   ├── engine.py        # High-performance vectorized/multiprocessing tournament runner (10,000+ matches)
│   │   └── metrics.py       # Win rate, expected points (EV), percentile ranking, and order-statistics trackers
│   └── analysis/
│       ├── __init__.py
│       └── order_stats.py   # Closed-form marginal trade math, continuous Nash checks, and 7-point pod locks
├── scripts/
│   └── run_tournament.py    # CLI entry point to run the 10,000-match benchmark & print the leaderboard
└── tests/
    ├── test_scoring.py      # Unit tests covering 1v1, 4-way ties, marginal wins, and conservation of payout
    └── test_validation.py   # Constraint enforcement unit tests
```

